#!/bin/bash

# (SCR)een (to) (P)ortable (P)ix(M)ap - (SCR2PPM)

The tiniest X11 screen capture aka. screenshot utility

# Install from flathub 

```
$ flatpak install io.github.igorlogius.scr2ppm
```

# Run via CLI 

```
$ flatpak run io.github.igorlogius.scr2ppm [ARGS]
```

# Options window

Starting the app without arguments (e.g. from the application menu) opens a small window
where you can choose what to capture (entire screen, a window or an area), an optional
delay and what to do with the screenshot. Pressing `Capture` (or `Enter`) closes the window
and starts the capture.

Checkboxes:
- `Save to file` saves the screenshot (format and folder can be chosen, they apply to this checkbox)
- `Copy to clipboard` puts the screenshot into the clipboard (always as PNG, whatever format is selected)
- `Show screenshot after capture` opens the saved file with your default image viewer (needs `Save to file`)
- `Re-open this window after capture`

At least one of `Save to file` and `Copy to clipboard` has to be checked, otherwise `Capture` is disabled.
All choices are remembered between runs.

Keyboard: `s`/`w`/`a` or `1`/`2`/`3` select the mode, `f` toggles save to file, `y` toggles copy to clipboard,
`v` toggles show, `r` toggles re-open, `p` cycles the format, `o` opens the folder, `c` changes the folder,
`Up`/`Down` change the delay, `Enter` captures, `Esc` cancels.

The wrapper script accepts `-o` (open), `-c` (copy to clipboard) and `-n` (don't save, use with `-c`) on its own,
e.g. `scr2ppm-wrapper -a -d 3 -c`.

# ARGumentS 

one of `-s`,`-a` or `-w` is required and `-d` can be optionally added to add a delay before the capture

```
  -s := capture the entire screen area
  -a := capture a custom area 
  -w := capture a window  
  -d := add a delay in seconds (optional) 
```

# Output 

The output will be send to STDOUT (STanDard OUTput) and can be written to a Portable PixMap (PPM) file 
or directly piped into another programm like (image/gaphickmagics `convert`) to process it further

# Examples 

```
  scr2ppm -s > shot.ppm		      // screenshot entire screen immediately 
  scr2ppm -s | convert - shot.png // make screenshot and save it via convert as a png
  scr2ppm -s -d 10 		          // screenshot entire screen after 10 seconds
  scr2ppm -a			          // screenshot selected area immediately
  scr2ppm -w -d 5		          // screenshot window (select with mouse) after 5 seconds
  scr2ppm -a -d 3		          // screenshot custom area after 3 seconds    
```
